{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790714353,"nonce":"/jhO8yDD71/+BvfFVykbOV7oOgI=","title":"Load modules referenced by bare class and enum values","message":"The dependency scan handled imports, type annotations, new expressions and class receivers in field access, but not a bare capitalized value. Type.getClassName(Xml) used a pre-registered class symbol without loading Xml.hx, so no Xml RTTI was registered and the call returned null. An explicit import Xml made the same probe pass. Issue9759 likewise failed with Cannot find name 'RootEnum' when a field initializer held that enum as a value.\n\nThe scanner now queues capitalized identifiers as candidate module dependencies, excluding ambient StdTypes names. The existing import loader resolves only names backed by source files and skips unresolved names. The no-import BareClassTokenDependency regression fails before this change and passes after it; TestReflect advances past Xml and next fails at Math, an extern class without a runtime RTTI entry.\n\nThe full tiered run scored 767/1094, up from 765/1094 in the preceding run. Issue9759 is the new pass; Issue10083 also returned to pass after varying across previous runs. All authored regressions and compiler Clippy pass. Workspace-wide fmt reports unrelated staged GPU files; the changed Rust file passes rustfmt.","files":null}]}